        "ui40": CheckGuide(proves: "Home's Where to? is a row of round icon buttons, and the line under them always says what is chosen.",
                           steps: ["Home, scooter not riding: you see up to 3 round buttons (2 at the biggest text size) and a dots button. The most visited places come first unless you pinned others.", "Tap one: it fills with the orange and the line reads, for example, Maya's house \u{2022} 12 mins \u{2022} 9% battery. Tap it again: No destination. If the battery is too low the line turns into the orange warning.", "Tap the dots: the full list opens. Settings app, Display, Text Size biggest: two buttons. VoiceOver reads the place name. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "ui41": CheckGuide(proves: "Each place can have its own icon and a place on Home.",
                           steps: ["Routes, Places, open a named place. Turn on Show on Home and pick position 1, 2 or 3; pick a symbol from the grid; then type MA in the letters box and tap Use letters.", "Go to Home: the place is on the quick dial with that icon. Back to automatic: the first letter of the name.", "Add a place by hand with a name: it is listed under Where to? on Home. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui42": CheckGuide(proves: "Where you were when the scooter last connected or disconnected is remembered, so the parked spot is right even when the app did not record a ride.",
                           steps: ["Take the phone and scooter somewhere new. Switch the scooter on and wait for Connected; switch it off.", "Scooter tab: the row reads Last seen here and a short time ago; tap it: the map shows where you were. Home's map pin is there too.", "Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .passive),
        "ui43": CheckGuide(proves: "Riding the app did not record is shown, not lost.",
                           steps: ["Ride a short way with Bluetooth off or the app force-quit, then open the app and connect.", "Home shows one line, for example 4.2 km ridden without recording, with Dismiss. Rides has a Not recorded section with the same distance.", "Settings, Report a problem: the log has a gap line saying how the app last ended. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .passive),
        "ui44": CheckGuide(proves: "The build number is visible on every screen without getting in the way.",
                           steps: ["Look at the very bottom of Home, Rides, Stats, Routes and Scooter: a tiny grey number such as 1.0 (229), centred between the tab bar and the home indicator.", "Open a screen without a tab bar (a place, Add a place): the same number at the same spot. Open a sheet (Where to? list): the number does not cover its content.", "Settings, About: the number matches. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "u100": CheckGuide(proves: "The speed sweet spot is found where your battery use per km is lowest, with an honest interval and honest what-if numbers.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: the sweet spot, the interval, High certainty, the honest baseline range, faster costs range, climbs left out and a flat curve hidden each say ok. How it looks is check ui61."], place: .noScooter),
        "u101": CheckGuide(proves: "The departure time and the battery-use creep insights find a real difference and stay quiet when there is none.",
