        "u120": CheckGuide(proves: "The charge timer's maths: the % now, when it is full, and when the full notification fires.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: 80 % at 23:34, full at 01:02, the notification at 01:24 (full plus the 5 % margin) and the limits at 0 and 100 each say ok."], place: .noScooter),
        "u121": CheckGuide(proves: "The targets (a battery %, km of range, a ready-by time) turn into the right % and time, and the two notifications say the right words at the right time.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: 10 km = 31 % at 19:57 (your % per km plus the 10 % margin and the reserve), the ready-by lines and the notification texts and times each say ok."], place: .noScooter),
        "u122": CheckGuide(proves: "The charge log keeps a measured charge (real % read on connect) apart from an estimated one (Unplugged), and draws gaps dashed.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: estimated, measured, solid and lighter bars, the dashed gap and the +32 % line each say ok. How it looks is check ui83."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui80": CheckGuide(proves: "You can say the scooter is plugged in, get a time to full, and see it on the Scooter tab and Home.",
                           steps: ["Switch the scooter off (so the app shows Connect). On the Scooter tab tap the outlined Plugged in pill next to Connect.",
                                   "The sheet shows Starting at N % with the time of the last reading. Tap the dots: Correct start % gives \u{2212} and +.",
                                   "Try the three modes under Also tell me when it has: Battery % (Off, 80, 90, Other), Range in km (type 10: it shows the % and the time), Ready by (pick a time). The line at the bottom shows Full \u{2248} and the notification time.",
                                   "Tap Start charging timer. The pill now says Unplugged; the card shows \u{2248} % with Full \u{2248}, the time left and a bar with a tick at 80 %. Open Home: the status pill says Charging with the full time and a thin bar.",
                                   "Tap Unplugged: everything goes back. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "ui81": CheckGuide(proves: "The charge shows on the lock screen (and the Dynamic Island) without opening the app.",
                           steps: ["Start the charging timer (check ui80), then lock the phone and wake the screen.", "A card: G2 charging, \u{2248} estimate, the \u{2248} % and Full \u{2248} time, a bar that fills by itself, the time left and when you plugged in. On a Dynamic Island phone: a bolt and the full time at the top.", "Unlock, tap Unplugged: the card goes. Tap Pass or Fail with a note (say if the % looked old: it updates when the app runs)."], place: .scooterHome),
        "ui82": CheckGuide(proves: "You get one quiet notification when the scooter should be full, and one at your target.",
                           steps: ["Start the timer with a start % near 90 (Correct start % in the dots) and a target (80 % cannot apply above it; use Range in km, or Off).", "Lock the phone. About 45 minutes later: G2 is full. Unplug when convenient. (it comes at the 100 % + 5 % time, a little after full).", "Start another timer and tap Unplugged: no notification comes. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "ui83": CheckGuide(proves: "The charge log is a chart you can read at a glance, and measured charges look different from estimated ones.",
                           steps: ["Scooter, then Battery, then scroll to Charge log.", "A line for the last 7 days, charge windows shaded orange, dashed where there was no reading, a dot for the last one. Below, Each charge: day and start time, a bar from the start % to the end %, +N % and how long.", "A charge you ended with Unplugged has a lighter bar and \u{2248}; one ended by connecting the scooter has a solid bar. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui60": CheckGuide(proves: "The Stats tab shows a few insights that change what you do, and none of the old ones.",
                           steps: ["Open Stats and scroll to the bottom. After a few weeks of rides you see an INSIGHTS section with up to 3 cards.", "Each card: a chip, a short headline, one big number, one action in a grey pill, Based on N rides. No Last week stats, no Peak °C, no Ride the same trip hints.", "With few rides you see only a quiet Still learning line, or nothing. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui61": CheckGuide(proves: "An insight's page explains it fully: what it means, your own data, what if, how it was worked out and how sure it is.",
                           steps: ["Stats → tap an insight card.", "Read top to bottom: the headline and 1-2 plain sentences; the chart of your own rides with dots, a curve, a band and a shaded area; What if; How we worked it out with the rides, km, dates, what was left out and the method in a box; How sure with the meter and the interval in words; Try this.", "Switch the phone to dark mode and look again. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui62": CheckGuide(proves: "The what-if numbers fit your own scooter and trips.",
                           steps: ["Stats → the sweet spot insight (or another one) → What if.", "The middle row's range is close to the range from full on the Battery page. Slower rows: more range, more minutes. Faster rows: less range, fewer minutes. The minutes fit your usual trip.", "If a number looks impossible, write it in the note. Tap Pass or Fail."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui63": CheckGuide(proves: "Home warns about a headwind only on the days it matters, with a % to leave with that includes the safety margin.",
                           steps: ["On a windy day (wind against you of 15 km/h or more on a usual ride), open Home before that ride.", "One TODAY card: Headwind on the way to …, +N % battery for the route, Leave … with at least M %, the wind and the time. Tap it: its page opens. Tap ×: it is gone until tomorrow.", "On a calm day there is no card; during a ride never. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .passive),
        "u90": CheckGuide(proves: "The sums in the info sheets add up from the numbers they show, for example 145.74 minus 0.27 is 145.47.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: the Money example, 300 made-up Money, Overall and Saved per km sheets and the Stats screen's own sheet each say ok. How they look is check ui52."], place: .noScooter),
        "u91": CheckGuide(proves: "The Past weeks chart on Stats has a bar for every week you rode, even a week with one riding day.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: four weeks of made-up rides give four bars with the empty week at 0, this week is not counted, and no rides give no chart."], place: .noScooter),
        "u92": CheckGuide(proves: "The scooter colour you choose on the Scooter tab is stored and comes back.",
                          steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: the six colours, the Sand default and the stored colour each say ok. The real thing is check ui50."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui50": CheckGuide(proves: "The Scooter tab starts with a big card with a line-art scooter, and you can recolour it.",
                           steps: ["Open the Scooter tab with the scooter switched off: a near-square card, the line-art scooter coming in from the left edge (about half of it inside), and on the right the name with a dot, the big battery %, When last connected and how long ago, the km pill and a round Connect button. Parked, Maintenance and Battery rows are below.", "Switch the scooter on: the dot turns green, the caption and the Connect button go away.", "Tap the dots at the top right: Rename scooter, Scooter colour, Choose photo. Open Scooter colour: six colours, a tick on the chosen one. Pick Ember: the line art turns orange at once. Close and reopen the app: still Ember. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "ui51": CheckGuide(proves: "You can put your own scooter picture on the card, and it stays on the phone.",
                           steps: ["Scooter tab, dots, Choose photo. Pick a picture of your scooter (a side view works best).", "P6-5: a Frame photo sheet opens with the whole photo (move and zoom it, then Save); it is kept as it is and fills the card. The name, battery %, km pill and Connect button turn light with a dark outline and are easy to read. Switch on Cut out the scooter for the old look: the scooter alone where the line art was, full card height, half inside from the left (check ui75 has the full steps).", "Try a picture that is already a cut-out (see-through background): it is used as it is. Dots, Remove photo: the line art is back. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui52": CheckGuide(proves: "Every info button opens the same kind of sheet, and the sums in them add up.",
                           steps: ["Stats: tap the info button next to Money. A short line, a box with Car fuel for N km, minus Electricity, equals Saved in orange, then Based on rows. The three numbers add up exactly.", "Tap a Based on row with an arrow, for example Car or Fuel price: the screen where it is set opens. Do the same for Overall and the Saved per km tile.", "Battery, Calibration and Charge log, and Settings, Costs: the same look, never more than one short sentence at the bottom. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui11": CheckGuide(proves: "On the phone, Add a place can be saved without hunting for a button, and no tab bar covers the fields.",
                           steps: ["Routes → Places → Add a place. Press and hold on the map to drop a pin (or tap the button to drop one in the middle).",
                                   "Type a name: Save in the top right turns on. Tap it, or press Return on the keyboard: the place is saved and the screen closes.",
                                   "The tab bar is not on screen. Open the place from the list: no tab bar there either. Settings → Costs → Price history: no bar under the fields.",
                                   "Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui12": CheckGuide(proves: "The Where to? list is a normal iOS sheet and the ride, route and place screens are a map with a normal scroll below.",
                           steps: ["Home, with a saved route: tap the Where to? row. A half-height sheet opens with No destination and each route with three chips. Swipe it down to close it; tap a route: it is chosen and the sheet closes.",
                                   "Open a ride, a route and a place: the map stays on top at a fixed height and the numbers scroll below it. Nothing can be dragged up or down.",
                                   "Scroll the numbers: the tab bar slides away, and comes back when you scroll up.", "Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui13": CheckGuide(proves: "Home has the big centred button with compact rows below it, and the scooter you parked shows on the map.",
                           steps: ["Look at Home with the scooter connected: the Start button is big and sits in the middle of the free space; the status pill is on top, the Where to? and Load rows are small, just above the tab bar.",
                                   "Ride somewhere, end the ride, switch the scooter off. Home's map shows a small orange scooter pin at the spot (when it is on the map picture); the Scooter tab shows \"Parked · place · time ago\".",
                                   "Tap that row: a map opens on the spot; the walking button opens Apple Maps.", "Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .ride),
        "ui14": CheckGuide(proves: "Stats has a Calendar / Rolling switch and the Overall section has the wide saved-per-km tile.",
                           steps: ["Stats: the small Calendar | Rolling switch is right of the title. Choose Rolling, then Month: the header reads LAST 30 DAYS, the arrow chip on Distance compares with the 30 days before. Leave the app and come back: Rolling is still chosen.",
                                   "Month, Calendar: the last label of the chart (the 31, or 30) is not cut off.",
                                   "Scroll to Overall: one wide tile with an orange value, \"/ km saved\" and \"every km by scooter instead of car\", next to CO₂; the ⓘ explains it.", "Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui15": CheckGuide(proves: "At the largest text size the Scooter card, the Routes list and the Rides rows stay on the screen.",
                           steps: ["Settings app → Accessibility → Display & Text Size → Larger Text: the largest size.",
                                   "Scooter: the status card spans the full width. Routes: the first row stays on the screen, the chip under the name. Rides: long rows wrap to two lines.",
                                   "Put the text size back. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .passive),
        "u110": CheckGuide(proves: "A place only shows a time when rides really ended there; otherwise it says why, and the place you stand in cannot be chosen.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: no ride gives \"no rides there yet\", one ride gives \"estimate after 2\", two rides give a time, and the place the phone is inside is marked here. How it looks is check ui70."], place: .noScooter),
        "u111": CheckGuide(proves: "The battery % the scooter reports for a few seconds after power-on (it says full) is not shown or sent.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: 100, 100, 100, 64, 64, 64 settles on 64, a really full scooter is believed after 8 s, and readings that never settle give a notification without a %. The real thing is check ui78."], place: .noScooter),
        "u112": CheckGuide(proves: "The Past weeks values and labels, the photo framing, the Home pins and the neutral arrival symbol work.",
                           steps: ["Developer → Checks → Run all automatic.", "Result: the four metric texts, a week made from rides, the photo cover rule, the 4th pin question, the glyph colours and the two symbols each say ok. How they look is checks ui73 to ui75."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui70": CheckGuide(proves: "The quick dial has a permanent No destination slot, shows each place in its own colour, and does not let you pick the place you are in.",
                           steps: ["Open Home (a few named places). The first round button is a dashed grey ring with ?. Tap a place: it fills in its colour (a dark symbol on light colours like yellow). Tap ?: the destination is cleared and the line says No destination.", "On the place screen change a place's colour: its Home icon follows. Stand in a place's circle (or use one you are at): its icon is dimmed with a small location mark; tapping it says \"You're at …\" and does not choose it.", "Every tap gives a light tick. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui71": CheckGuide(proves: "The Where to? list is compact, tells you why a place has no time, and lets you manage the quick dial.",
                           steps: ["Home → the … button. Each row is one line: icon, name, and on the right \"17 min · arrive 17:11\", \"no rides there yet\", \"1 ride there · estimate after 2\" or \"You are here\".", "Tap a pin: the place is On Home (a 4th asks which to replace). Tap Edit and drag the pinned places into order; Done. Close the sheet: Home shows the same order. On a place screen Show on Home agrees.", "Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui72": CheckGuide(proves: "The Places list is tidy and the charging switch has its words back.",
                           steps: ["Routes → Places: every card is the same full width and starts with the place's round icon in its colour (no map).", "Open a place: next to the plug it says \"I can charge here\". Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui73": CheckGuide(proves: "The Past weeks chart can show km, rides, time or ₪ saved, and each bar says what it is.",
                           steps: ["Stats → scroll to the Past weeks card. The title reads \"Past weeks · km\". Tap rides, time, ₪ saved: the pill slides, the bars change, the title follows. Close the app and reopen it: the choice is remembered.", "Every bar has its value on top and the week (for example 6 Sep) below, empty weeks too. Tap the title row: the page has a taller chart and the table. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui74": CheckGuide(proves: "The Scooter colour choice shows the real colours.",
                           steps: ["Scooter tab → the dots → Scooter colour.", "Six round swatches, each in its own colour (not all orange), a tick on the chosen one. Pick another: the scooter on the card changes and the sheet closes. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui75": CheckGuide(proves: "Your scooter photo is kept as it is, framed the way you like, with the cut-out as an option.",
                           steps: ["Scooter tab → the dots → Choose photo and pick a picture.", "The Frame photo sheet shows the whole photo in the card's shape. Drag to move it, pinch to zoom; it never leaves a gap. Tap Save: the photo fills the Scooter card with light text over it.", "Dots → Frame photo → switch on Cut out the scooter → Save: the old cut-out look. Switch it off again to get the whole photo. Dots → Remove photo brings the line art back. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui76": CheckGuide(proves: "The big Start button shows where you are going.",
                           steps: ["Connect the scooter, then on Home choose a place with the quick dial.", "The big disc shows that place's icon with the word Start under it, fading in. Tap ?: the usual start glyph returns. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "ui77": CheckGuide(proves: "Light mode looks warm and the build number never mixes with content.",
                           steps: ["Switch the phone to light mode. Home: a soft map behind the page with the parked pin, a warm glow behind the disc, quick dial and Load cards in warm sand.", "Stats, Rides and Scooter: cards and tiles are warm sand, no grey outline, a very soft shadow. Scroll a long list under the tab bar: the build number sits on a small pill and the list never shows through it.", "Note: Sunlight mode (bright screen outside) deliberately uses white panels. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui78": CheckGuide(proves: "The Scooter on notification and the battery % on Home and the Scooter tab are the real ones, not the boot value.",
                           steps: ["Lock the phone with the app in the background. Switch the scooter off, then on.", "The \"Scooter on · N%\" notification shows the % the scooter's dash settles on (not a stuck 100 %); if it cannot settle within 15 s it says Scooter on without a %.", "Open the app: Home and the Scooter tab show the same %. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "u130": CheckGuide(proves: "The battery % flip filter shows the lower of a 100 / 99 pair, and leaves a scooter that doesn't flip alone.",
                           steps: ["Developer \u{2192} Checks \u{2192} Run all automatic.", "Result: flipping readings show 99, clean ones pass unchanged, +1 waits 60 s, +2 shows at once. The real thing is check ui130."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui130": CheckGuide(proves: "The battery % no longer jumps between neighbours on the real scooter.",
                            steps: ["Switch the scooter on and watch Home for a minute: the % should not flip by one.", "After a ride open its battery chart: no zigzag. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .scooterHome),
        "u131": CheckGuide(proves: "A ride the phone recorded after the scooter's readings stopped making sense is kept, with the GPS distance and top speed.",
                           steps: ["Developer \u{2192} Checks \u{2192} Run all automatic.", "Result: 1.93 km of GPS is kept, under 300 m is not, the summary says Recorded by phone, the restore list holds 30 days. The real thing is check ui131."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui131": CheckGuide(proves: "A ride the app set aside can be brought back.",
                            steps: ["Rides \u{2192} scroll to the bottom \u{2192} Restore discarded ride.", "Find the 24 Oct 18:00 ride, tap Restore, tap Done: it is back in the list. Open it: Recorded by phone with a note. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .noScooter),
        "u132": CheckGuide(proves: "A short ride right after switching on never shows the battery going up (the boot reading is not used).",
                           steps: ["Developer \u{2192} Checks \u{2192} Run all automatic.", "Result: the boot 100 % never reaches the ride, and a ride whose end reading is higher shows its start once."], place: .noScooter),
        "u133": CheckGuide(proves: "A ride ends when you last moved, and a stop in the middle still counts in its Time.",
                           steps: ["Developer \u{2192} Checks \u{2192} Run all automatic.", "Result: the made-up ride ends at its last movement, its stop is kept and Time includes it."], place: .noScooter),
        "u134": CheckGuide(proves: "A ride starts when you really start riding, not when the scooter is switched on or wheeled out.",
                           steps: ["Developer \u{2192} Checks \u{2192} Run all automatic.", "Result: pushing first then riding starts at the first riding second, pushing only saves nothing, a lifted wheel is not riding. The real thing is check ui134."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui134": CheckGuide(proves: "Switching the scooter on early no longer starts the ride clock early.",
                            steps: ["Switch the scooter on at home (or in the lift) and wait a minute, or wheel it out.", "Ride as usual. Afterwards open the ride: its start time is when you set off. A minute of wheeling without riding saves no ride. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .ride),
        "u135": CheckGuide(proves: "A trip is judged by where it ends: the legs of an interrupted trip to a place you picked become one ride there, and odd rides do not bend the place's estimates.",
                           steps: ["Developer \u{2192} Checks \u{2192} Run all automatic.", "Result: Continue, merge, never-merge without a destination, closing, detour, the trim line and the widen offer each say ok. The real thing is check ui135."], place: .noScooter),
        "ui135": CheckGuide(proves: "An interrupted trip to a place you picked ends up as one ride there.",
                            steps: ["Pick a saved place on Home and ride part of the way; switch the scooter off for a few minutes.", "Home shows \u{21BB} Continue to that place: tap it and ride on to the place.", "The ride summary shows one ride with Includes a N min stop, trim it? Tap it, then Undo. Tap Pass or Fail with a note."], place: .ride),
        "u136": CheckGuide(proves: "A few bad scooter readings never throw away the ride, and the ride summary only mentions them when they changed a number you see.",
